  "summary_en": "Hong Kong subsidiary legislation under the Road Traffic Ordinance establishing a pilot licence and AV certificate regime for autonomous vehicle trials, with Commissioner powers, testing, insurance, journey data, incident reporting, offences and Transport Tribunal review.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Pilot licence (up to 5 years) required to run AV schemes, with fit-and-proper and public-interest safety tests",
   "Per-vehicle AV certificates (max 12 months) require roadworthiness, risk analysis and third-party insurance",
   "Commissioner may require demonstration, testing and inspection of AVs",
   "Pilot proprietors must keep journey data and operation records and report defects, malfunctions and accidents",
   "Decisions reviewable by Transport Tribunal; offences for interference with AVs and non-compliance"
